WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.969
Joe: We weighed iconic
fast-food-menu items

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:06.339
in the US and the UK and
compared their prices

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.275
to see which country is
getting the most for its money.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.844
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:19.319
In the UK, a small cheese
pizza will cost you £11.99,

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.588
which is around $15.54.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:24.958
That's a price per square
inch of 21.8 cents.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:25.959
Small in the US?

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:29.662
$9.49, which is about 12
cents per square inch.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.097
I know I got a small,

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.499
but apparently they're also doing

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:33.867
small peppers with the small pizzas.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.535
Look how small this is.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.171
Skimping on the peppers, eh, Papa?

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:39.906
An XXL cheese pizza in the UK

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:42.976
will cost you around $23.32,

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:46.312
which is a price of 12.3
cents per square inch.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:50.717
USA's extra large? $15.49.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.218
That cannot be right.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.653
Sprinkle a little math on that,

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:57.824
that's 7.7 cents per square
inch. That is so cheap.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.359
So, what can we take away from this?

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.293
Well, in both countries,

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:02.695
the more pizza you buy,
the cheaper it gets.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.631
In the US, the price per
square inch of a small

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:07.300
is 55% more than an extra large.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:12.305
And in the UK, it shoots
up to a huge 77% more.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.339
I mean, it makes sense, right?

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:14.207
I mean, that's how they get you.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.910
They pretty much are tricking
you into getting more pizza

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.978
'cause it's cheaper per
square inch, so you're going,

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.580
"Oh, I'll just get the
extra large instead."

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.982
And then a year later, you're fat.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.653
"Whoops! It was such a good deal!"

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.363
Harry: In the UK, that's
$1.95 per 100 grams.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:40.700
In the US, that's $2.36 per 100 grams.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.770
That makes them 21% more
expensive in the US.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.737
And we're going to weigh the Big Mac

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.573
and see if there is
any difference in size.

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.708
I'm not sure there will
be, but let's find out.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.649
Find out how much a large
fries weighs in the UK.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.891
That's a cost of $1.94
per 100 grams in the UK.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.460
That makes them 14% cheaper in the US.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:11.764
Next up for the US is our large,

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.334
which is a 14-inch diameter.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:17.804
Harry: 100 square inches of
pizza in the UK would cost $15.

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:22.142
100 square inches of pizza
in the US would cost $9.70.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:25.245
That makes it 35.3% cheaper in the US.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.515
We want to make sure that
you're getting the same amount

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:31.151
of filling as you do in
the US here in the UK.

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:34.187
So what we've got here is
a foot-long Italian BMT

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:37.457
on hearty Italian with lettuce and olives.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.058
We're going to weigh it
to see if the quantities

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.960
are the same. All right.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:41.961
BMT.

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:52.805
We're going to weigh the large fries

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.208
to see the comparison between UK and US.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:01.948
That makes them 15% more
expensive in the US.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:11.858
Per 100 grams, the US
Whopper is 6% cheaper.

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:20.833
This is a crunchy beef
Taco Supreme in the UK.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:24.270
The UK price is $5.18 per 100 grams.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.173
That makes it 49% cheaper in the US.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:29.209
This is a UK chicken quesadilla.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:36.716
That's 27% cheaper in America.

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:38.651
This is a Crunchwrap Supreme in the UK.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.027
This has an estimated weight,

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.263
and it should weigh 146 grams

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:52.966
if the website's ingredients
information is correct.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:55.134
But ours actually weighs 154 grams.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.903
So we're actually getting
more than expected.

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:04.377
We're about a hair over 150. OK.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:06.546
We're going to weigh the
cup and then also the extras

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:08.681
to see if what you get really is a bonus

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:11.985
or if it actually all adds
up to the supposed total.

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:15.121
165.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.156
So, first, we'll do the scale, right?

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:19.759
So this is supposed to be 411 grams.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.261
Let's see what we got.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:23.329
What is this? 170?

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.398
Woof, guys, that's not even close.

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:26.833
So, our regular cup of fries

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:29.068
actually only contained 165 grams,

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:31.371
which is less than half of
what you're supposed to get.

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:32.872
We're going to weigh the rest of the fries

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:35.608
to see if that makes up the difference.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:36.976
So, even with all the bag fries,

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:39.145
which we assigned to the regular portion,

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.447
we're still only looking at 276 grams,

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:42.849
which is well below the portion size

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:44.550
you're supposed to be
getting for a regular.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.420
Excellent idea, Harry. I will do the same.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:51.224
Now we are up to ... 275?

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:53.626
Still not even — it's supposed to be 411?

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:56.029
So it looks like we've been a
bit shortchanged on the fries.

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:57.964
Because it was all given
to us in one big bag,

00:04:57.964 --> 00:05:00.099
it's hard to tell which
portion came out small.

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.200
So what we're going to do is

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.102
add the little fries to this one,

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:05.138
get a total figure for all three portions,

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.139
and then figure out how much

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:08.207
we've been shortchanged overall.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.175
So, we've done the maths,

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:12.011
and between our large,
regular, and little fries,

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:15.381
including the bag fries,
we only got 830 grams.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:19.185
However, we were supposed
to get 1,220 grams,

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:22.422
which means we've been shortchanged
by roughly a third here.

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:23.823
Joe: With the rest of the bag fries,

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.892
the large, and the little.

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:30.697
So they gave us 851 grams of fries

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:31.864
total.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:35.134
They're supposed to give us 1,225.

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:36.536
Hey, Siri,

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:39.772
851 is what percentage

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:42.475
of 1,225?

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:45.812
Siri: About 69.4693%.

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:47.480
69%.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.449
Nice.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:51.451
So, at least in our case, it seems as if

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:54.620
the generosity of Five Guys
has been a bit overstated.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.656
Maybe they just overfill
smaller containers,

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:58.891
so you kind of think you're
getting more than you should be,

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.460
whereas in reality, if you measure it all,

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.228
you're actually maybe getting less.

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:10.136
So, we're going to weigh
this burrito half at a time

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:11.371
to see what the total is.

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:20.880
In the UK, we can only get
one size of guac on the side.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.248
It's supposed to be 4 ounces.

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:24.150
We're going to measure it
to check if that's the case.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:28.121
That's a price of $3.58
per 100 grams in the UK.

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:30.790
The US version is therefore 26% cheaper.

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:36.329
So, which country gets
more pizza for its money?

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:39.298
In the UK, a large cheese pizza

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:41.467
will cost you £15.99.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:44.837
That's a price of 15
cents per square inch.

00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:48.040
The US large hand-tossed
cheese pizza is about $13.99,

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.543
which is about 9 cents per square inch,

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:55.148
